B.dKv=new A.t("link",B.S,'Optional { table, fromId, type } \u2014 when a recurring row completes and materializes a next-occurrence copy, also writes a relations-style edge {fromId, toId: <newId>, type} into `link.table` so the copy enters a subtreeClosure walk from `fromId` (type defaults to "contains"). `fromId` resolves via resolveValueToken at fire time ($setting:<key> etc \u2014 empty/unresolved skips the link, logged, never a crash or dangling edge). Alternatively { table, inherit: true, type } copies EVERY incoming `type` edge of the SOURCE row onto the copy instead of a static fromId \u2014 the recurrence lands in whichever board(s) the source actually belongs to. Omit `link` for no edge.',B.f,null,!1)
