B.avC=new A.t("swipeActions",B.S,'Swipe-left reveal buttons. Builtins ["edit","delete"] (default), or objects { label, icon, action, role:"danger" }; label may be a {lang: text} map. false/[] disables.',B.f,null,!1)
B.HY=new A.t("confirmDelete",B.W,"Ask to confirm before a swipe/menu delete removes a row (default off).",B.f,null,!1)
B.dAK=new A.t("builtinDelete",B.W,"Set false to suppress the engine's own row Delete everywhere it would otherwise appear (long-press row menu AND the default \"delete\" swipe entry) \u2014 default true, exact prior behavior when omitted. Use when the applet declares its OWN guarded delete (e.g. confirms an item count, refuses when shared) so a more-discoverable built-in Delete can't bypass it and orphan data.",B.f,null,!1)
B.dvO=new A.t("bubbles",B.S,'Opt-in chat-bubble row styling: { byColumn, selfValue, example }. Rows whose byColumn value matches the resolved selfValue (a literal, or a token like $playerId / $rowId / $selected:<table>) render end-aligned + tinted ("me"); everything else (including an unset selfValue token) renders start-aligned + neutral ("them"). Absent entirely -> the plain ListTile row, unchanged. Optional `example: { ids: [...], label, hideLabel, chipLabel, hiddenFromSetting, onHide }` marks demo-content rows (house-design-rules.md rule 10): each listed row id gets a small "example" chip (chipLabel, localizable), a slim label+divider (label, localizable) renders once above the first such row with a Hide action (hideLabel + onHide, an action spec), and when the named `hiddenFromSetting` board setting resolves truthy (\'1\'/\'true\') those rows are dropped from the list entirely.',B.f,null,!1)
B.zS=new A.t("emptyIcon",B.C,"Icon name shown atop the empty-state panel (when the source has no rows).",B.f,null,!1)
B.zY=new A.t("emptyTitle",B.C,"Headline for the empty state; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.f,null,!0)
B.zT=new A.t("emptyText",B.C,"Body text for the empty state; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.f,null,!0)
B.zH=new A.t("emptyAction",B.S,"Action spec { fn, args } (or bare-string fn) fired by the empty-state button \u2014 e.g. add the first row.",B.f,null,!1)
B.zP=new A.t("emptyActionLabel",B.C,'Label for the empty-state action button (default "Add"); may be a {lang: text} map.',B.f,null,!0)
B.zJ=new A.t("emptyActionIcon",B.C,'Icon name for the empty-state action button (default "add").',B.f,null,!1)
B.HZ=new A.t("example",B.S,'Opt-in demo-content marking: { ids, column, label, chipLabel, hideLabel, hiddenFromSetting, onHide }. Exactly one of `ids` (a list of row ids) or `column` (rows where this column is truthy) selects the marked rows \u2014 both or neither makes the block invalid and it is ignored. Marked rows get a small "chipLabel" chip (default "Example"); a slim "label" divider (default "EXAMPLES") renders once above the first marked row with a "hideLabel" (default "Hide") action. `onHide` is an optional action spec { fn, args } fired through normal dispatch; when absent, tapping Hide writes `board.settings[hiddenFromSetting] = true` directly \u2014 no host code required. When the named `hiddenFromSetting` board setting resolves truthy (\'1\'/\'true\'), marked rows are dropped from the node entirely. All labels may be a {lang: text} map.',B.f,null,!1)
