B.dLX=new A.t("filter",B.S,'Opt-in row scope for `nodesTable` (and, unless `dataFilter` overrides it, `dataTable` too) \u2014 same shape as `bubl`\'s filter: {column, value} or {column, in:[...]}; `value`/each `in` entry may be a token ($selected:<table>, $rowId, $playerId). Absent = all rows (unchanged behavior); resolved value/set EMPTY = no rows, never all. A step/data row freshly created while a resolved scalar {column, value} filter is scoping the view is stamped with that column:value so it stays in scope (e.g. a model-scoped flow: `{"column":"model_id","value":"$selected:models"}`).',B.f,null,!1)
